identifier: KKBlocks
name: KKBlocks
abstract: Six shapes, seven sizes and twelve colours of save-compatible static building blocks for Kerbal Konstructs.
description: |-
  KKBlocks adds 42 ready-to-place static objects for Kerbal Konstructs, so
  you can build bases, launch-site scenery, ramps and decorative structures
  without importing models. It covers six shapes (cube, 45-degree ramp,
  pyramid, cylinder, dome and sphere) in seven sizes (0.5, 1, 2, 4, 8, 16
  and 32 m). Each static ships twelve colours through the stock TextureSet
  system, giving 504 combinations that can be switched at any time in the
  Kerbal Konstructs instance editor.

  The original cube statics keep their exact names and mesh files, so
  existing saves and placed instances keep working. Every mesh uses one
  stock-like KSP/Diffuse material and a single submesh; the origin sits at
  the bottom centre, so objects scale upward from the ground. Ramps,
  pyramids, cylinders and domes have solid convex mesh colliders, cubes have
  a box collider and spheres have a sphere collider, making ramps drivable
  and spheres able to roll. There is no plugin, no ModuleManager patch and
  no runtime model generation: the .mu files are produced offline by the
  included MuTool source.

  Requirements: Kerbal Space Program 1.12.x and Kerbal Konstructs 1.12.x.
  Those are the only hard dependencies - no texture packs, no plugins and
  no other mods are needed. Visual mods such as Scatterer, EVE, TUFX or
  Deferred are optional. KKBlocks is save-compatible and can be installed
  or removed at any time; placed instances remain in the Kerbal Konstructs
  save data.

  Need help or want to share a build? Join the Discord:
  https://discord.gg/GEjdeqJE6g

  Licensed under MIT: you may use, modify and redistribute it, including in
  mod packs, as long as the copyright and license notice are kept.
author: Lynx
$kref: '#/ckan/github/ehemaliger56-debug/KKBlocks'
ksp_version: 1.12
license: MIT
